From ba95f56b2931a9c419e95b7a367b51012086f00f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:12:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): memory noun shortcuts + passthrough fix (P1,
 febf7690)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wire remember/recall/insights as VISIBLE back-compat aliases of the
canonical `memory <sub>` form in lib/commands/_aliases.js. The memory
noun (add/recall/search/insights) shipped in PR #392 (issue 25362344),
so P1's remaining deliverable is the alias wiring, not the noun itself.
Per owner ruling the canonical write verb is `memory add` (no `save`).

- remember -> memory add, recall -> memory recall, insights -> memory
  insights; all visible, none deprecated.
- Add passthroughAliasNames() (issue-canonical only) + visibleAliasNames();
  switch bin/forge.js passthrough to passthroughAliasNames() so the memory
  shortcuts are NOT in the bd flag-passthrough set — keeps bare
  `recall -p <dir>` / `recall --help` byte-identical.
- remember/recall/insights stay registered command files, so resolveDispatch
  never rewrites them — bare-verb dispatch is byte-identical.
- forge --help: memory shows as a noun; remember/recall/insights render in a
  new Shortcuts block (trimmed from Additional commands).

Refs febf7690, epic eea186fa.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
